    {"id": "open-door-home", "s": "May your home be full of coming and going this Eid, with one more bowl of sheer khurma ready for whoever walks in.", "m": "The best Eid homes are the ones where the door stays open all day and nobody is allowed to leave without eating.", "l": "That kind of generosity is the real spirit of the day. May Allah keep your home just as open and just as full, today and in all the ordinary days that follow."},
    {"id": "hugs-mend-distance", "s": "May the hugs after Eid namaz this year close a few distances that words couldn't.", "m": "Eid has a quiet way of making it easier to reach out, to forgive, and to start the conversation we kept putting off.", "l": "I hope this Eid brings you that kind of peace: the lightness of letting go of old grudges, and the warmth of being welcomed back by someone you've missed."},
    {"id": "duas-accepted", "s": "On this Eid, may every dua you make, spoken aloud or kept in your heart, be heard and answered in the best way.", "m": "Not always in the way we expect, perhaps, but in the way that turns out right for us.", "l": "May Allah grant you patience while you wait, gratitude for what has already been given, and the peace of knowing you are cared for."},
    {"id": "sharing-with-needy", "s": "May your Eid be full of the joy that comes from sharing, especially with those who need it most.", "m": "A full plate means more when someone else's plate is full too, and Eid teaches that beautifully.", "l": "I hope the generosity of this day stays with you all year in small ways: a meal shared, a kind word, a helping hand that nobody else notices."},
    {"id": "barakah-everyday", "s": "May Allah put barakah in your home this Eid: in your food, in your time and in the work of your hands.", "m": "Barakah isn't always about having more; often it's about what you have feeling like enough.", "l": "I pray this Eid leaves you with that sense of contentment, a heart at ease, and days that are simple, full and quietly blessed."}
