    {"id": "eidi", "s": "No matter how old you are, I hope someone still hands you Eidi this year, and that you accept it without pretending to refuse.", "m": "Though the little 'no, no, keep it' drama before taking the envelope is a tradition of its own.", "l": "And if you're now the one giving Eidi, may your wallet stay strong and the children's smiles make every note worth it. Here's to an Eid full of these small, happy exchanges."},
    {"id": "biryani-invites", "s": "May your Eid be full of biryani invitations, and may you have the stomach space to accept every single one.", "m": "There's a special Eid skill in saying 'I'll just have a little' and then quietly going back for a second plate.", "l": "May your hosts be generous, the mutton be tender, and the conversations around the dastarkhwan go on long after the plates are cleared."},
    {"id": "tailor-on-time", "s": "May your new Eid clothes come back from the tailor on time this year, and actually fit.", "m": "Every year someone is rushing to the tailor's shop the night before Eid, and every year the tailor promises 'just one hour'.", "l": "Whatever you end up wearing, may you look your best, feel even better, and spend the day with people who would welcome you in any outfit."},
    {"id": "eid-forwards", "s": "Look after your phone this Eid, because the family WhatsApp group is about to send the same glittering Eid image forty times.", "m": "Somewhere behind those forwards, though, are elders and old friends who simply want you to know they remember you.", "l": "So this year, answer a few of them with a real call. A familiar voice on Eid morning is worth more than a hundred greeting cards, glittery or not."}
